# @akili-spec changes/cicd-executor-poc design §4.1, DD-19, DD-23
# Repo-root .dockerignore: used when the Executor image is built with the
# REPO ROOT as build context (`docker build -f executor/Dockerfile .`), so
# that deployment-definitions/, schemas/ and deploy-scripts/ are addressable
# by the build (design DD-19: "copied into the image at build time"), while
# local-only analysis files and anything not needed inside the image never
# reach the build context in the first place.
#
# executor/.dockerignore is the separate, executor-scoped ignore file used
# when the build context is `executor/` instead (e.g. the T-01 falsifier
# fixtures, built with --dockerfile against an executor-root context) — it
# is NOT superseded by this file.

# Local-only analysis files (never versioned — design.md §4.1, premise P-26).
JENKINS_REPLACEMENT_AKILI_CONTEXT.md
JENKINS_REPLACEMENT_FEASIBILITY_ANALYSIS.md

# Node / JS
**/node_modules
executor/dist
coverage

# Specs, runbooks and docs are not runtime content.
docs/

# VCS and local tooling state.
.git
.codegraph
.local

# OS cruft.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
